      "text": "To solve for \\( x \\) in the equation \\( x^2 = 729 \\), we start by taking the square root of both sides of the equation. This gives us:\n\n\\[\nx = \\sqrt{729}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to determine the value of \\( \\sqrt{729} \\). We know that \\( 729 \\) is a perfect square. Let's find the prime factorization of \\( 729 \\):\n\n\\[\n729 = 27 \\times 27 = (3 \\times 3) \\times (3 \\times 3) = 3^4\n\\]\n\nTaking the square root of \\( 3^4 \\) is equivalent to:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{3^4} = 3^{4/2} = 3^2 = 9\n\\]\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n\\[\nx = 9\n\\]\n\nSince \\( x \\) is positive, the value of \\( x \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{9}\n\\]",
